1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,210
Four themes.

2
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:10,976
Innocence to experience: the confident child of the first half becomes someone who has seen what she cannot explain, and it happens exactly at I know not.

3
00:00:10,976 --> 00:00:16,809
Nature as theatre: she never looks at the sun itself, only at what it does.

4
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:24,505
Death, handled gently: Dickinson wrote dozens of poems about dying, and this is one of the few that is not afraid.

5
00:00:24,505 --> 00:00:29,921
And faith and doubt: the church and the shepherd are all there, but only as what seemed.

6
00:00:29,921 --> 00:00:32,708
A comforting picture, and an honest verb.

